<workout_file>
	<author>Jarvis Chau (via TrainingPeaks)</author>
	<name>Sweet Spot (45 mins)</name>
	<description>One of TrainingPeaks Virtual&apos;s classic workouts:
Sweet Spot Training.

The perfect go-to workout; warm-up, 32 minutes just enough below your FTP to get a really good workout, but without becoming over-tired, and then you&apos;re done. Simple, but effective.</description>
	<sportType>bike</sportType>
	<tags/>
	<workout>
		<Warmup Duration="300" PowerHigh="0.73" PowerLow="0.53">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
10:Welcome to Sweet Spot;
20:This classic workout is perfect for improving your FTP.;
30:Just 32 minutes of work - 4 minutes on, 4 minutes off, four times.;
60:For now, focus on warming up, and getting your legs spinning.;
150:Half way through the warmup.;
240:1 minute to go.;
}"/>
		</Warmup>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.95">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Bring the power up to just below your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
180:1 minute to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.85">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Just ease off the power slightly.;
10:Keep the legs spinning.
Focus on recovery at pace.;
180:1 minute to go until we take it back up again.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.95">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Second set.
Back to just below your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
180:1 minute to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.85">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Just ease off the power slightly.;
10:Keep the legs spinning.
Focus on recovery at pace.;
180:1 minute to go until we take a short rest.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.55">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Focus on recovering as much as you can.;
10:Keep the legs spinning.
Grab a drink.;
180:1 minute to go until we take it back up again.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.95">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Third set.
Back to just below your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
180:1 minute to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.85">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Just ease off the power slightly.;
10:Keep the legs spinning.
Focus on recovery at pace.;
180:1 minute to go until we take it back up again.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.95">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Fourth and final set.
Back to just below your FTP now.;
60:First minute done.
Good job.;
180:1 minute to go.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<SteadyState Duration="240" Power="0.85">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:Just ease off the power slightly.;
10:Keep the legs spinning.
Focus on recovery at pace.;
180:1 minute to go until we&apos;re done for the day.;
}"/>
		</SteadyState>
		<Cooldown Duration="240" PowerHigh="0.53" PowerLow="0.73">
			<textevent timeoffset="0" message="!TextEvents:{
0:...and relax.;
30:Take on some fluids and start to wind it down.;
60:There&amp;apos;s 3 minutes left until the end.;
70:The power will ramp down slowly while you recover.;
180:Great job today.;
190:Looking forward to working out with you again soon.;
}"/>
		</Cooldown>
	</workout>
</workout_file>